@startuml security-layers
'==============================================================================
' Figure (Chapter II, Security): defence in depth. Concentric controls guard
' the immutable event log at the core; each layer holds even if an outer one is
' bypassed. The data-layer control (database row security) is a comby v3
' affordance that CLMPilot does not yet activate -- one of the Chapter IV seams.
' Render:  plantuml -tpdf security-layers.puml   (or -tpng)
'==============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam rectangle {
  roundCorner 10
  BorderColor #6B6B8A
  FontColor #1A1A2A
}

rectangle "Network perimeter\nTLS edge; stores on an internal-only network" as net #EDEDF6 {
  rectangle "Authentication\nrevocable server-side session; admin email one-time code" as auth #E0E0EE {
    rectangle "Authorization\nper-tenant RBAC, enforced at dispatch" as rbac #D2D2E4 {
      rectangle "Tenant isolation\ntenant context on every command, query and event" as tenant #C4C4DA {
        rectangle "Immutable event log\nsystem of record = audit trail" as core #B0B6DE
      }
    }
  }
}

note right of tenant
  Database row security (comby v3)
  reinforces this layer but is not
  yet activated.
end note
@enduml
